This analysis presents the measurement of four specific semileptonic $B_s^0$-meson decays involving electron-neutrino and muon-neutrino pairs: $B^0_s 	o e^-\overline{
u}_X D^{*+}$, $B^0_s 	o e^-\overline{
u}_X D^+$, $B^0_s \mu^-\overline{
u}_X D^{*+}$, and $B^0_s \mu^-\overline{
u}_X D^+$. Derived from proton proton collisions collected by the LHCb experiment at $\sqrt{s}$ = 13 TeV, these are categorized based on the charge of the accompanying neutrino. Utilizing an end-point method, branching fractions for these rare processes are determined. The resulting figures align with theoretical predictions within both inclusive and exclusive frameworks. Furthermore, this study estimates the $B_s^0$-meson lifetime by leveraging precise external values for relevant semileptonic decay rates. The obtained metrics are then employed to constrain free parameters within various particle physics extensions designed to account for anomalies and search for mechanisms operating beyond the Standard Model.
